<title>INDIA: India allows fresh investment by AT&amp;T unit.</title>
<headline>India allows fresh investment by AT&amp;T unit.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1996-10-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Indian government said on Friday that a unit of U.S. telecommunications group AT&amp;T Corp has been allowed to raise its equity stake in a cellular telephone venture by 3.31 billion rupees.  </p>
<p>The government said in a statement that the Cabinet Committee on Foreign Investment on Thursday approved a proposal by Birla AT&amp;T Communications Ltd for increased equity in cellular mobile telephone services.</p>
<p>It said the proposal was for an increase in the equity stake held by AT&amp;T Cellular Private Ltd to 5.88 billion rupees from 2.57 billion, following an increase in paid-up capital to 12.0 billion rupees from 5.25 billion.</p>
<p>-- New Delhi newsroom +91-11 301 2024</p>
</text>
